# Component page content

When authoring or editing files in `content/components/`, follow [content/COMPONENT-PAGE-PATTERN.md](content/COMPONENT-PAGE-PATTERN.md).

## Tracks

- **Bespoke** (Button, Alert & Banner): full vault + `<!-- demo -->` + `demos/{slug}-demos.tsx`
- **Hybrid** (all other components): vault `description` + `## Overview` (+ optional sections); Storybook stories = variation sections via `components.$slug.tsx`

Scaffold hybrid pages: `npm run scaffold:components`. Refresh description/Overview: `npm run refresh:component-content`.

## Page description

Frontmatter `description` renders under the h1. Write **1–2 sentences** describing the component and where it is used — not ports, file paths, or technical caveats (those go in Overview or Code).

## Section order

1. **Overview** (required, no demo)
2. **Variation sections** (1+, usually with demo) — bespoke: markdown + demo; hybrid: route injects Storybook iframes per story
3. **Guidelines** (optional, no demo)
4. **Dimensions** (optional, bullets + demo)
5. **Typography** (optional, usually demo)
6. **Props** (optional)
7. **Related components** (optional, prose + demo) — last optional section
8. **Code** (required, always last)

Skip optional sections when not applicable. Do not reorder required blocks.

## Variation section format (bespoke)

```markdown
## {Product-language name} {#id-if-needed}

- **{Variant}** — {when/where in production}.

<!-- demo -->
```

Hybrid pages: do not duplicate story sections in markdown — only list story ids in `toc`.

## Demo placement

- Default: bullets then demo at section end.
- Spacing is automatic (`DocSectionStack`) — do not add blank lines for rhythm.

## Markdown vs code

**Bespoke:** demos in `src/components/docs/demos/{slug}-demos.tsx`.

**Hybrid:** Storybook iframes + code badges in `components.$slug.tsx`. Optional vault sections (Guidelines, Related) are prose-only unless extended later.

**Figma:** `component-figma-links.ts` — hybrid route reads registry automatically.

Reference: `content/components/alert-bar.md`, `content/components/button.md` (bespoke); `content/components/avatar.md` (hybrid).
